{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

<section class="pageHero wrap">
  <p class="label">Join Us</p>
  {# "You" names a party, so it takes that party's color rather than one of the
     five payoff accents — those are spoken for, one per page. #}
  <h1><span class="c-hu">You</span> only need one corner to start.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The work sits between people, agents, and buildings. Almost nobody arrives
    knowing all three — we haven't hired anyone who did. Come in from whichever
    corner you already know.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ===== Three ways in ============================================== -->
<section class="band band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">Three ways in</p>
    <h2>Where you're coming from, and what you'd pick up.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid--2">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-bl">You know buildings</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
        Building physics, HVAC, energy modeling, construction. You understand why
        a room behaves the way it does.
      </p>
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">You'd pick up</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How to make an agent reason about a system you already understand</li>
        <li>Sensing and data pipelines</li>
        <li>Running studies with human participants</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-ai">You know AI</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
        Machine learning, language models, multi-agent systems, control. You can
        build something that decides.
      </p>
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">You'd pick up</p>
      <ul>
        <li>What a building actually is, physically and thermally</li>
        <li>Why the constraint set is harder than it looks</li>
        <li>Why an explanation matters as much as an action</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-hu">You know people</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
        Human factors, physiology, survey design, public health. You know how to
        find out what someone actually experiences.
      </p>
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">You'd pick up</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The engineering vocabulary to make your findings actionable</li>
        <li>Instrumentation and measurement</li>
        <li>How occupant data becomes a control decision</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head">You're not sure yet</p>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
        You're an undergraduate, or switching fields, and the above sounds
        interesting but unfamiliar.
      </p>
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">That's fine</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everyone in the lab started without one of the three</li>
        <li>Curiosity and follow-through matter more than a checklist</li>
        <li>Knock on Dr. Jung's door and we'll work out where you fit</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== What we offer ============================================== -->
<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">What we offer</p>
    <h2>The HUBS lab will be fully committed to your success.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid--2">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-ai">You will become a knowledge HUB of</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Human–AI–Building interaction</li>
        <li>Agentic and physical AI for the built environment</li>
        <li>Occupant behavior, comfort, and health in buildings</li>
        <li>Building | community | urban energy modeling</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="card__head c-ai" style="margin-top:1.75rem">In so doing, let's</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Build the vision for your career</li>
        <li>Set up milestones during your course</li>
        <li>Have weekly individual meetings with Dr. Jung</li>
        <li>Have monthly group meetings to learn from your peers</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-bl">You will be exposed to</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Multidisciplinary research across all three corners</li>
        <li>Machine learning, language models, and multi-agent systems</li>
        <li>Sensors, networks, and embedded electronics</li>
        <li>Physics-based simulation and real building data</li>
        <li>Human-subject study design and ethics review</li>
        <li>Scientific thought processes</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== What we expect ============================================= -->
<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">What we expect</p>
    <h2>Prepared to become a HUB.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid--2">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-hu">Attitude — this part is not negotiable</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Be motivated and passionate</li>
        <li>Devote yourself to research and be responsible for it</li>
        <li>Be curious about new knowledge and willing to learn</li>
        <li>Be positive and interactive with peers</li>
        <li>Be willing to work outside the field you arrived with</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-hu">Skills — helpful, not required</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Background in building science, or in ML, or in human factors</li>
        <li>Research experience with tangible outcomes</li>
        <li>Programming experience (Python, R)</li>
        <li>Experience with LLMs, agents, or reinforcement learning</li>
        <li>Electronics experience (e.g. Arduino, Raspberry Pi)</li>
        <li>Building energy modeling experience</li>
        <li>Excellent English verbal and written communication</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout" style="margin-top:2rem">
    <p>
      Nobody has all of the above, and we don't expect you to. Tell us which parts
      you have and which parts interest you — that's a more useful message than a
      list of everything you've ever touched.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== Programs =================================================== -->
<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">Programs</p>
    <h2>Where you might fit.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="defList measure">
    <div class="defList__item">
      <p class="defList__term">Ph.D. program</p>
      <p class="defList__meta">Imagine yourself becoming a faculty member after graduation.</p>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <p>
          It seems like a long journey, taking more than three to four years. However, once you
          become aware of where you'd stand after graduation, it might not be long. You will gain
          the privilege of applying for an assistant professor position — a role that requires you
          to get funding, conduct your research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, mentor
          graduate students, and serve your communities.
        </p>
        <p>
          To become a strong candidate, it is highly recommended to publish more than three journal
          articles as the main contributor when you apply. The HUBS lab will guide you to accomplish
          your goals during this course.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="defList__item">
      <p class="defList__term">Master's program</p>
      <p class="defList__meta">You are becoming a researcher.</p>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <p>
          A researcher creates knowledge. You understand the body of knowledge and scientifically
          create the necessary knowledge for peers or the public. By being involved in research
          projects led by the HUBS lab, you will become not only a researcher, but also a HUB.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are interested in a Ph.D. degree, it is highly recommended to publish one journal
          article. This experience will prepare you to become a successful scholar.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="defList__item">
      <p class="defList__term">Bachelor's program</p>
      <p class="defList__meta">You get the taste of becoming a researcher.</p>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <p>
          Are you interested in research, but do not know where to start? Consider knocking on
          Dr. Jung's door at any time. By being involved in research projects led by the HUBS lab,
          you will have a better idea of conducting a study, discovering knowledge, and penetrating
          the current body of knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are interested in graduate-level degrees, it is highly recommended to participate
          in publication efforts. This experience will prepare you to know more about becoming a
          researcher.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

